==> emb --help <==
usage: emb [-h] [--version] <command> ...

Let Claude lead AI coding workers on this machine.

positional arguments:
  <command>
    choices   read settings and choices, claim or set them
    engines   show whether each engine is connected, or its models
    run       start a worker run, or work with one
    gapcheck  review a plan for undefined or contradictory behaviour
    flow      plan, start, watch and answer flows
    panel     ask several models one question and collect their answers
    ground    print what to read before choosing a worker
    merge     merge a reviewed worker branch, then clean it up
    cleanup   remove merged worker branches, their worktrees and sessions
    prune     remove old ended run, flow and panel records
    deps      show the installed and newest version of each dependency
    app       start the desktop app, or bring it forward
    skill     install or remove the ember skill for Claude Code

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --version   show program's version number and exit
==> emb choices --help <==
usage: emb choices [-h] [--json] [--id ID] [--claim] [--finish ID]
                   [--request KEY=VALUE] [--set KEY=VALUE] [--clear KEY]
                   [--once KEY=VALUE] [--clear-once] [--expect-generation N]

Read settings and choices, claim or release a one-time choice, or set settings
and one-time choices at a terminal.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --json                print JSON (every reply is JSON)
  --id ID               the run's claim id
  --claim               claim the pending one-time choice
  --finish ID           release the claim for ID
  --request KEY=VALUE   a request-layer value, with a read or --claim
  --set KEY=VALUE       save a standing setting
  --clear KEY           remove a standing setting
  --once KEY=VALUE      set the one-time choice for the next run
  --clear-once          remove the pending one-time choice
  --expect-generation N
                        refuse the write unless the generation is N
==> emb engines --help <==
usage: emb engines [-h] [--refresh] [--json] [--models ENGINE]

Show whether Codex, OpenCode and Claude Code are installed, signed in and
connected, or list one engine's models.

options:
  -h, --help       show this help message and exit
  --refresh        check the engines, or read the model list, instead of the
                   cache
  --json           print JSON
  --models ENGINE  print ENGINE's model list (codex, opencode or claude)
==> emb run --help <==
usage: emb run [-h] [--engine ENGINE] [--dir DIR] [--task-file FILE]
               [--model MODEL] [--effort EFFORT] [--read-only] [--read PATH]
               [--trailer LINE] [--claim ID] [--window] [--send RUN]
               [--message-file FILE] [--screen RUN] [--interrupt RUN]
               [--attach RUN] [--close RUN] [--force] [--recover RUN]
               [--status [RUN]] [--json] [--quiet] [--stall MINUTES]

Start one worker in its own worktree and tmux session and wait for its turn,
or send to, read, interrupt, close or recover a run. Each non-zero exit prints
a next: or owner: line.

options:
  -h, --help           show this help message and exit

start a run:
  --engine ENGINE      codex, opencode or claude
  --dir DIR            a folder in the git checkout
  --task-file FILE     the brief
  --model MODEL        the model (default: menu)
  --effort EFFORT      the effort (default: menu or engine)
  --read-only          work in the checkout, edit nothing
  --read PATH          a path the run may read; repeatable
  --trailer LINE       a trailer line for each commit; repeatable
  --claim ID           read the menu with this claim id
  --window             also open a terminal window on the session

work with a run:
  --send RUN           send a message and wait for its turn
  --message-file FILE  the message
  --screen RUN         print the session's screen
  --interrupt RUN      interrupt the current turn
  --attach RUN         open a new window on the session
  --close RUN          end the session; keep worktree and branch
  --force              with --close: close even while busy or holding messages
                       Ember did not send; with --send: send even to a session
                       holding such messages
  --recover RUN        collect a turn that ended unwatched
  --status [RUN]       print a run's record, or every run's
  --json               with --status: JSON

waiting and output:
  --quiet              print only the first line and summary
  --stall MINUTES      minutes without a screen change before exit 124
                       (default 10)
==> emb gapcheck --help <==
usage: emb gapcheck [-h] --plan FILE [--dir DIR]
                    [--engine {codex,opencode,claude}] [--model MODEL]
                    [--effort EFFORT] [--claim ID] [--read PATH] [--window]
                    [--stall MINUTES] [--json] [--brief] [--reply FILE]
                    [--confirmed]

Review a plan in one read-only run, print its brief, or read a reply from
another worker.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --plan FILE           the plan
  --dir DIR             checkout folder (default: .)
  --engine {codex,opencode,claude}
                        reviewer engine
  --model MODEL         reviewer model
  --effort EFFORT       reviewer effort
  --claim ID            the existing claim id
  --read PATH           an additional readable path; repeatable
  --window              open a run window
  --stall MINUTES       minutes without a screen change before exit 124
                        (default 10)
  --json                print a JSON result
  --brief               print the brief only
  --reply FILE          read an existing reply
  --confirmed           run the check although the gap check settings skip or
                        ask
==> emb flow --help <==
usage: emb flow [-h] [--plan FILE] [--dry-run] [--start] [--watch FLOW]
                [--status [FLOW]] [--lead FLOW TASK] [--resume FLOW]
                [--cancel FLOW] [--reason TEXT] [--writer W] [--reviewer W]
                [--claim ID] [--stall MINUTES] [--send FILE] [--accept]
                [--commit SHA] [--review] [--worker W] [--drop] [--json]

Run a JSON task plan in waves with writers, read-only reviews and fix rounds.
Accepted tasks merge into a flow branch. Each non-zero exit prints a next: or
owner: line.

options:
  -h, --help        show this help message and exit
  --plan FILE       the JSON task plan
  --dry-run         print workers and waves
  --start           start the flow runner
  --watch FLOW      wait for a lead stop or end
  --status [FLOW]   show one or all flows
  --lead FLOW TASK  answer a task's lead stop
  --resume FLOW     restart a flow's runner
  --cancel FLOW     cancel a flow's runner
  --reason TEXT     the cancellation reason
  --writer W        writer engine:model[@effort]
  --reviewer W      reviewer engine:model[@effort]
  --claim ID        read choices with this claim
  --stall MINUTES   minutes without a screen change before a task stops
                    (default 10)
  --send FILE       send a correction to the writer
  --accept          accept the task branch
  --commit SHA      the commit to accept
  --review          start a fresh review
  --worker W        replace the writer with W
  --drop            drop the task
  --json            print JSON
==> emb panel --help <==
usage: emb panel [-h] [--question-file FILE] [--dir DIR] [--member W]
                 [--claim ID] [--read PATH] [--stall MINUTES]
                 [--timeout MINUTES] [--dry-run] [--status [PANEL]]
                 [--recover PANEL] [--retry PANEL MEMBER] [--close PANEL]
                 [--json]

Ask members the same question in parallel read-only runs and write a summary
of their answers. Each non-zero exit prints a next: or owner: line.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --question-file FILE  the question as UTF-8 text
  --dir DIR             a checkout folder (default: current folder)
  --member W            engine:model[@effort]; repeatable
  --claim ID            read choices with this claim
  --read PATH           an additional path members may read; repeatable
  --stall MINUTES       minutes without a screen change (default 10)
  --timeout MINUTES     panel deadline in minutes (default 30)
  --dry-run             validate inputs and print resolved members
  --status [PANEL]      show one or all panels
  --recover PANEL       collect unfinished members without asking again
  --retry PANEL MEMBER  ask a failed or not-started member again
  --close PANEL         close every open member run without force
  --json                print JSON
==> emb ground --help <==
usage: emb ground [-h] [--dir DIR] [--json]

Print the machine, the Claude Code surface, Claude Code's worktree.baseRef
setting and the folder's checkout, branch, dirty state, remote and instruction
files.

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --dir DIR   the folder to read (default: the current one)
  --json      print JSON
==> emb merge --help <==
usage: emb merge [-h] --into TARGET [--verdict VERDICT] --note TEXT
                 [--dir DIR] [--json]
                 BRANCH

Merge a reviewed branch into a local branch with a merge commit, in the
worktree that has the target checked out, then remove the branch, its run's
worktree and session as emb cleanup does. Never pushes. Each non-zero exit
prints a next: or owner: line.

positional arguments:
  BRANCH             the reviewed branch

options:
  -h, --help         show this help message and exit
  --into TARGET      the branch to merge into
  --verdict VERDICT  the lead's verdict; only keep merges
  --note TEXT        the verdict line, printed first and kept in the merge
                     commit
  --dir DIR          a folder in the git checkout
  --json             print JSON
==> emb cleanup --help <==
usage: emb cleanup [-h] --merged-into TARGET [--branch BRANCH] [--dir DIR]
                   [--dry-run] [--json]

Remove each Ember run branch the target contains, its run's worktree and
session, and keep everything else with a reason and the command that resolves
it. Each non-zero exit prints a next: or owner: line.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --merged-into TARGET  the branch the worker branches were merged into
  --branch BRANCH       only this branch
  --dir DIR             a folder in the git checkout
  --dry-run             report what would be done; change nothing
  --json                print JSON
==> emb deps --help <==
usage: emb deps [-h] [--refresh] [--json]

Show each component Ember depends on: its installed version, the newest
version its source offers, its status and the command that updates or installs
it. Newest versions are read when the cached ones are six hours old or more,
or with --refresh.

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --refresh   read newest versions now, even when the cached ones are recent
  --json      print JSON
==> emb app --help <==
usage: emb app [-h] [--hidden]

Start Ember's desktop app, or bring the running one forward. With --hidden it
starts in the tray; without a tray the window shows.

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --hidden    start in the tray, with the window hidden
==> emb skill --help <==
usage: emb skill [-h] <action> ...

Install, remove or show the ember skill for Claude Code. The skill is a link
at $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/skills/ember, or ~/.claude/skills/ember when
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR is unset or empty, to the skill source: the source
checkout's skill/ folder when emb runs from a checkout, else
/usr/share/ember/skill. Each non-zero exit prints a next: or owner: line.

positional arguments:
  <action>
    install    link the skill into Claude Code's skills folder
    uninstall  remove the skill's link
    status     print the link, its state, its target and the skill source

options:
  -h, --help   show this help message and exit
==> emb skill install --help <==
usage: emb skill install [-h] [--force] [--json]

Create the link to the skill source. A broken link is replaced; a link to
another folder only with --force; a folder or file is never touched.

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --force     replace a link to another folder
  --json      print JSON
==> emb skill uninstall --help <==
usage: emb skill uninstall [-h] [--json]

Remove the link when it points to an Ember skill or to nothing. A folder or
file is never touched.

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --json      print JSON
==> emb skill status --help <==
usage: emb skill status [-h] [--json]

Print the link, its state, its target and the skill source.

options:
  -h, --help  show this help message and exit
  --json      print JSON
